# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; this example file is not.

# --- SEO audit: Core Web Vitals ---
# Google PageSpeed Insights API key. Used by the SEO audit's `pagespeed` check.
# Without it the check rate-limits against the shared public quota and scores 0
# (a measurement error, NOT a real CWV failure).
#
# Get one (free):
#   https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library/pagespeedonline.googleapis.com
#   -> Enable "PageSpeed Insights API" -> Credentials -> Create API key
#
# Then re-run the SEO audit (it also accepts --api-key <key>).
# The user's global keys live in ~/.env — adding it there works too.
PAGESPEED_API_KEY=
